  {
   "approach": "The summit road (Highway 5) is seasonal and closed in winter, so in the cold months the approach adds a long walk up the road or in from Echo Lake via the Chicago Lakes basin. From the Summit Lake parking area, follow the wide trail toward the notch opposite the Tan Buttresses, then descend leftward into the cirque to the foot of the nearest buttress. Several gullies lead toward the ridge; this is the rightmost of them, just right of the Micro Goulotte. The two routes merge after the start into a moderate snow gully with mixed steps leading to the ridgeline. These are steep snow slopes in avalanche terrain, so check the avalanche forecast first.",
