  {
   "approach": "This climb is on the true north face and is entered from above. Drive to the summit, then rappel from the true summit (the highest point, with the USGS marker) down onto a snow-covered ramp below the climb. Wear a helmet, since the face is loose in places and gets no sun. The summit road (Highway 5) is seasonal and closed in winter, so in the cold months the approach adds a long walk up the road or in from Echo Lake via the Chicago Lakes basin. These are steep snow slopes in avalanche terrain, so check the avalanche forecast first.",
